      "text": "To find the probability that four fair 6-sided dice will not all show the same number, we can first calculate the probability that they will all show the same number and then subtract this from 1.\n\nThere are 6 possible outcomes for each die (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6), so the probability that four dice will all show the same number is 1/6.\n\nTherefore, the probability that not all dice will show the same number is 1 - 1/6 = 5/6.",
